# Line endings for the native sources under compiler/.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS SCOPED TO ONE DIRECTORY.
#
# The tree is checked out on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, and the same tree
# is built and measured from WSL over /mnt/c. That combination has already cost
# a real bug once: reading the working copy from the Linux side made every text
# file look modified, so a "is the tree dirty?" flag saturated to true and
# carried no information.
#
# The fix for compiler/ is to take the ambiguity away for the files that get
# compiled and hashed: they are LF on disk everywhere, so a digest taken on one
# side matches a digest taken on the other.
#
# It is deliberately NOT `* text=auto`. A repository-wide rule would renormalise
# every tracked file on the next checkout, which moves the bytes of the shipped
# bundles — the one thing the release-time invariants exist to keep still.
compiler/** text eol=lf
